Sony Xperia XZ Permium JP Verison Customized Kernel.
  For SO-04J/G8188 stock Android PIE ROM

  defconfig using:
    maple_dcm_defconfig
  if need force 4k:
    maple_dcm_4k_defconfig

Features:
   eas(walt)
   PSI
   And see commits....

How to build kernel:

  Prerequisites:

    * The ARM cross-compiler
      You can use prebuild executable binary which is included in
      standard Android repository. Please visit to external site.
      In case of this platform, we recommend to use gcc 4.9 or later
      such as aarch64-linux-android-4.9 to avoid known issues.
      
      [LineageOS/gcc4.9/aarch64](https://github.com/LineageOS/android_prebuilts_gcc_linux-x86_aarch64_aarch64-linux-android-4.9)
      [LineageOS/gcc4.9/arm](https://github.com/LineageOS/android_prebuilts_gcc_linux-x86_arm_arm-linux-androideabi-4.9
      (branch lineage-19.1 test passed)
      
    * In emp-remastered please use clang compiler

    * [Clang](https://android.googlesource.com/platform/prebuilts/clang/host/linux-x86/)
    (r530567 test passed)
    

  Step 1: Build Your Kernel
    $ cd <your-kernel-dir>

    $ export ARCH=arm64

    $ make maple_dcm_defconfig O=./out

    $ PATH="<path to clang folder>/bin:<path to 64-bit gcc folder>/bin:<path to 32-bit gcc folder>/bin:${PATH}" \
      make -j$(nproc --all) O=out \
                      ARCH=arm64 \
                      CC=clang \
                      CLANG_TRIPLE=aarch64-linux-gnu- \
                      CROSS_COMPILE=aarch64-linux-android- \
                      CROSS_COMPILE_ARM32=arm-linux-androideabi- 
          

    You can see arch/arm64/boot/Image-dtb if you succeed in building.


  Step 2: Repack to flashable zip
    (In the Linux Kernel directory)
    (In test,flash location is FOTAKernel.Please manual modify updater-script
    $ ./repack

  Step 3: Manually modify init.rc in boot.img
  	refer:https://android.googlesource.com/platform/system/core/+/c638569c2ebdc36f93a05190cd52dc08f4321d1b%5E%21/#F0
  	https://android.googlesource.com/platform/system/core/+/3280e48847e5dd16521ad7040d53eb30b66bf740
  	https://android.googlesource.com/platform/system/core/+/f8a7e37b2de50eb7a2bcd59b305adb8f68f204c1%5E%21/#F0
  	https://android.googlesource.com/platform/system/core/+/64d97d87611a39163aa121f17214f4a846954cee%5E%21/#F3
  	
  Step 4: If cannot bootable,selinux set to permissive 
  	
